From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alastair D'Silva <alastair@d-silva.org>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +1000
Subject: clk: sunxi-ng: a733: Add peripheral bus clocks and resets

Add clock gate, parent multiplexer, and reset definitions to ccu-sun60i-a733.c
for peripheral buses and system controllers, and export their IDs in the A733
CCU devicetree binding headers.

On Allwinner A733, peripheral bus gates and reset registers are relocated
into distinct register banks compared to earlier sunxi generations:
- DMA controller (0x704), Hardware Spinlock (0x724), and Message Box (0x744)
- Enhanced PWM bus gate and module clocks (0x784, 0x78c)
- UART0 through UART7 bus clock gates and resets (0xe00 - 0xe1c)
- I2C0 through I2C7 bus clock gates and resets (0x1e80 - 0x1e9c)
- SPI0 through SPI2 bus clock gates and resets (0xf00 - 0xf14)
- Infrared RX and TX controllers (0x1004, 0x100c)

Without these clock and reset definitions in the CCU driver, device drivers for
serial consoles, I2C PMICs/sensors, SPI flash, hardware spinlocks, and DMA
fail during probe when acquiring their devicetree clock and reset resources.

Signed-off-by: Alastair D'Silva <alastair@d-silva.org>
Assisted-by: Antigravity <antigravity@google.com>

